<protocol name="view_image" type="tool_mastery" domain="shared">

## PURPOSE

Master the view_image tool - multimodal image viewing for visual analysis.
This tool gives you EYES. Returns multimodal content so you SEE images directly.

## CRITICAL CONCEPT

view_image returns the actual image in your context. You don't get a description -
you SEE the image visually, like looking at a photograph. This enables:

- Direct visual analysis (materials, colors, textures, dimensions)
- Feature identification (patterns, labels, defects)
- Item categorization based on appearance
- Quality verification before data operations

---

## WHEN TO USE

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| User provides image | view_image IMMEDIATELY |
| Before write_data | Visual verification of attributes |
| After image processing | Quality check before using output |
| Material identification | See textures, finishes, transparency |
| Duplicate detection | Visual comparison when names ambiguous |
| Item categorization | Visual features determine type |

---

## PARAMETERS

### image_path (required)

Image source - accepts multiple formats:

| Format | Example | Source |
|--------|---------|--------|
| Storage path | `inbox/thread_id/photo.jpg` | download_media output |
| Storage path | `pending/thread_id/edit.png` | image processing output |
| Local path | `/path/to/image.jpg` | Local files |
| URL | `https://example.com/image.jpg` | Direct URLs |

**Storage Path Convention:**
- `inbox/` - User uploads via download_media
- `pending/` - Processed images from image tools

---

## WHAT YOU SEE

When you call view_image, you receive:

1. **Text metadata**: Source type, original size, format
2. **Image block**: The actual image rendered in your context

You can then analyze:
- Item type (shape, form factor)
- Material (texture, transparency, finish)
- Features (patterns, labels, markings)
- Size estimates (relative proportions)
- Quality (lighting, clarity, condition)
- Style (premium, standard, industrial)

---

## COMMON PATTERNS

### Pattern 1: Data Entry Analysis

User sends image for data entry. View first, then enrich.

```python
# Step 1: SEE the item
view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_123/item.jpg")
# You see: [visual details - type, material, features]

# Step 2: Research enrichment (based on what you saw)
research_product(query="[item type] [material] specifications")

# Step 3: Duplicate check
read_data(table="items", search_patterns={"name": "%keyword%"})

# Step 4: Create entry
write_data(...)
```

### Pattern 2: Image Processing Quality Check

After processing, verify output quality.

```python
# Step 1: Process image
image_tool(operation="process", source="inbox/thread_123/raw.jpg")
# Output: pending/thread_123/processed.png

# Step 2: Verify quality
view_image(image_path="pending/thread_123/processed.png")
# You see: [processing result - verify quality acceptable]

# Step 3: Use in data entry (if quality good)
write_data(...)
```

### Pattern 3: Visual Comparison for Duplicates

Names similar, need visual confirmation.

```python
# Query returns potential duplicate
read_data(table="items", search_patterns={"name": "%keyword%"})
# Found: "Similar Item" - is this the same?

# Visual comparison
view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_123/new_item.jpg")
# You see: [visual details of new item]

# Existing item image (from asset_url)
view_image(image_path="https://storage.example.com/items/existing.jpg")
# You see: [visual details of existing item - compare]
```

### Pattern 4: Material Identification

Need to identify material from visual appearance.

```python
view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_123/unknown.jpg")
# You see: [visual characteristics]
# Analysis: Based on transparency, texture, finish - likely [material type]
```

---

## VISUAL ANALYSIS FOCUS AREAS

When viewing images, focus on:

### Material Indicators
- Transparency level (clear, translucent, opaque)
- Surface finish (glossy, matte, textured)
- Color characteristics (natural, pigmented)
- Flexibility cues (rigid, semi-flexible)

### Item Features
- Shape (cylindrical, rectangular, custom)
- Components (closures, attachments)
- Labels/branding (text, logos)
- Textures (smooth, patterned, ribbed)

### Quality Signals
- Image clarity (sharp vs blurry)
- Lighting (even, shadows, reflections)
- Background (clean, cluttered)
- Item condition (new, damaged, dirty)

### Size Estimation
- Proportions relative to known objects
- Hand-scale if present
- Label text size as reference

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

### Wrong: Assuming Without Viewing

```
WRONG:
User: "Here's my item image" [inbox/thread_123/item.jpg]
Agent: "I'll process this as a [assumed type]..."
# Never viewed the image - assumption may be wrong!

CORRECT:
User: "Here's my item image" [inbox/thread_123/item.jpg]
Agent: view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_123/item.jpg")
# Now I SEE: [actual visual details]
Agent: "I can see this is a [actual type] with..."
```

### Wrong: Metadata Only

```
WRONG:
# Skipping view_image, just reading filename
"Based on 'item_type_500.jpg' filename, this is [assumption]"
# Filename could be wrong!

CORRECT:
view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_123/item_type_500.jpg")
# You SEE: [actual content - verify filename accuracy]
```

### Wrong: Batch Viewing

```
WRONG:
# Trying to view multiple images at once
view_image(image_path=["img1.jpg", "img2.jpg", "img3.jpg"])

CORRECT:
# View one at a time
view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_123/img1.jpg")
# Analyze first image...
view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_123/img2.jpg")
# Analyze second image...
```

### Wrong: Repeated Viewing

```
WRONG:
view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_123/item.jpg")
# ... later in same conversation ...
view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_123/item.jpg")  # Same image again!

CORRECT:
view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_123/item.jpg")
# Remember what you saw, don't re-view unless image changed
```

---

## IMAGE SIZE HANDLING

- Original images auto-resized to 1024px max dimension
- Quality preserved (LANCZOS resampling)
- RGBA/LA converted to RGB (white background)
- Output: JPEG at 80% quality for efficient tokens

This means you see a faithful representation, but:
- Fine text may be harder to read
- Very small details may be lost
- Good enough for identification and material analysis

---

## RETURN STRUCTURE

### Success

Returns multimodal content blocks:

```json
[
  {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Image (url): 1024x768, JPEG"
  },
  {
    "type": "image_url",
    "image_url": {"url": "data:image/jpeg;base64,..."}
  }
]
```

You SEE the image in your context after the text metadata.

### Error

```json
[
  {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Error: Image not found at inbox/thread_123/missing.jpg"
  }
]
```

---

## PROACTIVE VIEWING

When user mentions an image, VIEW IT IMMEDIATELY:

```
User: "I uploaded a photo to inbox/thread_789/new.jpg"
Agent: [IMMEDIATELY calls view_image before any other action]
Agent: "I can see your item - it's a [description]..."
```

DO NOT:
- Ask "can you describe the image?"
- Wait for explicit "please view the image"
- Make assumptions without viewing

